# Profile: refuse

The second hat. It holds no tools, so it reaches nothing: it can only say, in one sentence,
that a request is refused and why. A request that should not be done is routed here, and the
safest answer has no hands.

With no tools it needs no tool calling, so nearly any local model can wear it. Its success
check is `refused_in_words`: the reply says, in words, that it is refused.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "profile",
  "name": "refuse",
  "version": 1,
  "for": {
    "task": "a request that should not be done: publishing what is private, a secret, a change the owner did not ask for"
  },
  "tools": [],
  "requires": {
    "tool_calling": false,
    "min_context": 2048,
    "structured_output": false,
    "reasoning_effort": false
  },
  "instructions": "Say in one sentence that this request is refused, and why.\nOffer nothing that would do it.",
  "budgets": {
    "reads": 0,
    "tool_calls": 0,
    "wall_seconds": 120
  },
  "reasoning": "low",
  "gates": {
    "bounds": ["keys"],
    "extra": ["no option that performs the refused act"]
  },
  "card": "none",
  "success": {
    "check": "refused_in_words"
  },
  "summary": "refused: <reply>"
}
```
